.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1029 AM PDT Tue Sep 15 2026

MVFR-IFR conditions continue directly along the coastline with VFR
across the interior. MVFR stratus returns again tonight with IFR
conditions possible directly along the coastline. Confidence is
low to moderate that stratus will not reach SJC or LVK overnight
but if it does occur, it likely will not be until after 09Z.
Highest potential for IFR conditions directly along the coastline. Onshore
winds pick up this afternoon to around 10-15 knots with light to
variable southerly winds overnight.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR through the rest of today with MVFR CIGs
likely to return overnight. Patchy stratus could arrive as early
as 04Z but it more likely will not arrive until 10Z. Onshore winds
to around 15 knots expected this afternoon and evening with
occasional stronger gusts possible. Stratus clears by late
tomorrow morning with a return of onshore winds around 15 knots
expected during the afternoon and evening.

SFO Bridge Approach...Generally similar to SFO but gusts may be
slightly stronger (closer to 20 knots) over the bay on the Bridge
Approach.

Monterey Bay Terminals...MVFR-IFR conditions persist at MRY
through the rest of today. Confidence is low that a ceiling will
fully mix out at MRY due to persistent onshore push of stratus
into MRY from the Monterey Bay region. If stratus does clear, it
likely will not be until after 19Z. MVFR-IFR CIGs return to SNS
overnight. Winds remain light through mid morning with westerly
winds around 12 knots expected today. Winds weaken overnight
becoming light to variable.

