.FIRE WEATHER...
Issued at 345 AM PDT Tue Sep 15 2026

The transport of cooler air on northwest winds relative to sea
surface temperatures in the upper 50s to lower 60s continues to
help produce coastal stratus early this morning. The marine layer
depth varies from 1500 to 2000 feet. Above the marine layer
temperature inversion, humidities are currently in the mid 20% to
30% range. The depth of cool air transport will increase which
will gradually increase humidities at higher elevations during mid
to late week. Before humidities reach a maximum, there may be
temporary, small areas of nocturnal drying at highest elevations,
coverage though should be minimal.

